Temporal Considerations

The timing of evidence must be considered under multiple frameworks:

      Pre-existing reputation evidence (relevant to baseline damages);

     Contemporaneous evidence during alleged defamation (relevant to actual malice);

     Subsequent evidence showing impact (relevant to causation).

Authentication and Chain of Evidence

      For social media and electronic evidence, authentication requirements can be satisfied through

multiple methods:

      Direct testimony from witnesses with knowledge (Rule 901(b)(1));

      Distinctive characteristics and circumstantial evidence (Rule 901(b)(4));



